WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:03.560
- We are raging upwards
in terms of the emissions

00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:05.020
on the planet

00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:06.383
and we've got to turn that around.

00:00:06.383 --> 00:00:08.966
(upbeat music)

00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:21.610
Increasingly, I've see
CEOs of major companies

00:00:21.610 --> 00:00:23.100
around the world,

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:25.940
beginning to move spontaneously

00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:28.270
to commit their companies

00:00:28.270 --> 00:00:29.690
to net zero,

00:00:29.690 --> 00:00:31.290
to decide on

00:00:31.290 --> 00:00:33.760
when if they're in an
investment firm or bank,

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:36.450
how much they can land
or what they can invest

00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:40.520
in climate related emissions
reduction activities.

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:42.980
So I think there's a huge
new market opening up.

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:44.580
I think it's very exciting

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:45.670
and in my judgment,

00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:47.940
it's gonna be the biggest
market we've seen in the world

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:49.790
since the industrial revolution.

00:00:49.790 --> 00:00:51.220
- Do you have to drive

00:00:51.220 --> 00:00:53.110
that like your work with other countries

00:00:53.110 --> 00:00:54.720
and in setting emissions goals?

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:56.440
How does that tie in

00:00:56.440 --> 00:00:58.120
to the private sector type trends

00:00:58.120 --> 00:00:59.420
that you're talking about?

00:01:00.590 --> 00:01:02.260
- The private sector

00:01:02.260 --> 00:01:04.620
will ultimately, obviously,
make its own decisions

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:08.250
but what we're trying to
do is galvanize groups

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:10.730
of entities to come together

00:01:10.730 --> 00:01:14.020
in order to challenge other companies

00:01:14.020 --> 00:01:15.370
and other corporations.

00:01:15.370 --> 00:01:16.630
Why are we doing that?

00:01:16.630 --> 00:01:19.540
Because there's no way any government

00:01:19.540 --> 00:01:22.100
will find or has the trillions

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:24.670
of dollars necessary to
affect this transition.

00:01:24.670 --> 00:01:26.400
And when you add up

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:28.530
the other entities

00:01:28.530 --> 00:01:30.170
that are coming to the table,

00:01:30.170 --> 00:01:32.300
we have the potential

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:34.230
of huge amounts of capital going

00:01:34.230 --> 00:01:37.110
into alternative, renewable fuels,

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:40.450
possibly hydrogen exploration,
get green hydrogen.

00:01:40.450 --> 00:01:43.820
You have the possibilities
of a storage of one kind

00:01:43.820 --> 00:01:46.020
or another which could
change the entire game.

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:49.180
Just as people have for
years in venture capital bet

00:01:49.180 --> 00:01:51.020
on some particular technology

00:01:51.020 --> 00:01:53.580
or disruption in the marketplace,

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:55.620
that's gonna happen now
in the energy sector

00:01:55.620 --> 00:01:57.570
because people feel compelled

00:01:57.570 --> 00:01:59.870
to try to address this challenge.

00:01:59.870 --> 00:02:01.850
And governments are
gonna create incentives

00:02:01.850 --> 00:02:03.180
for some of that capital and move

00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:05.790
in certain directions. For instance,

00:02:05.790 --> 00:02:07.030
President Biden is planning

00:02:07.030 --> 00:02:10.470
to build 500,000 charging
stations in America

00:02:10.470 --> 00:02:12.190
which will certainly begin

00:02:12.190 --> 00:02:14.520
to make it more possible
for people to feel good

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:16.870
about buying electric and transitioning.

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:19.130
There will be a transition
in the auto industry.

00:02:19.130 --> 00:02:20.100
GM has announced,

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:23.410
they're gonna only produce
electric vehicles by 2035.

00:02:23.410 --> 00:02:24.300
Ford is moving

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:26.600
in a similar direction,
Mercedes, Volkswagen.

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:29.640
Car companies around the
world are setting dates

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:31.370
for when they will no longer be making

00:02:31.370 --> 00:02:32.730
an internal combustion engine.

00:02:32.730 --> 00:02:34.960
- A lot of that is
driven by market forces.

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:37.380
Your job is to negotiate
with the other countries

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:39.930
of the world, presumably on...

00:02:39.930 --> 00:02:41.830
Emissions reduction targets--

00:02:41.830 --> 00:02:45.180
- We can say that affects the
market force that becomes...

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:46.570
Part of the transition in the market.

00:02:46.570 --> 00:02:47.780
If all of a sudden...

00:02:47.780 --> 00:02:48.657
What happened in Paris?

00:02:48.657 --> 00:02:53.550
(speaks in foreign language)
(crowd applauds)

00:02:53.550 --> 00:02:55.920
196 countries came together.

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:57.240
They all decided,

00:02:57.240 --> 00:02:59.650
they were each gonna pursue their own plan

00:02:59.650 --> 00:03:02.070
but they were all gonna reduce emissions.

00:03:02.070 --> 00:03:03.750
That meant that they have

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:05.300
to find the means of doing so

00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:07.020
and in the first year after Paris,

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:09.340
and second year after Paris,

00:03:09.340 --> 00:03:11.600
several hundreds of
billions of dollars went

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:13.810
into alternative, renewable investment.

00:03:13.810 --> 00:03:15.360
That's the direction we were moving

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:17.870
until President Trump stopped the momentum

00:03:17.870 --> 00:03:19.300
by pulling out of the agreement,

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:22.030
and he gave license to
some reluctant countries

00:03:22.030 --> 00:03:23.790
to sort of pull back

00:03:23.790 --> 00:03:25.640
but we will regain that now.

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:27.950
- You mentioned President
Trump and his withdrawal

00:03:27.950 --> 00:03:30.950
on a lot of environmental
regulations, of all the rollbacks,

00:03:30.950 --> 00:03:32.230
but a lot of the private sector trends

00:03:32.230 --> 00:03:34.090
that we're talking about
continued on, anyway.

00:03:34.090 --> 00:03:36.530
That investment grew exponentially.

00:03:36.530 --> 00:03:38.379
Coal-fired power plants closed.

00:03:38.379 --> 00:03:40.230
Things like this happened
all around the world.

00:03:40.230 --> 00:03:41.950
- And not enough in enough places.

00:03:41.950 --> 00:03:44.130
- So then, what is success for you?

00:03:44.130 --> 00:03:46.350
Do you think that figuring out new numbers

00:03:46.350 --> 00:03:48.970
for every country, more ambitious numbers

00:03:48.970 --> 00:03:50.160
will lead to this?

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:50.993
Do you need to see

00:03:50.993 --> 00:03:52.540
the private sector
investment already follow?

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:54.730
How do you define success?

00:03:54.730 --> 00:03:56.150
- Well, success will be

00:03:56.150 --> 00:03:58.090
the vast majority of nations,

00:03:58.090 --> 00:04:00.360
coming to the table in Glasgow

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:02.640
and putting down plans

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:03.700
for how they're going

00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:06.730
to target net zero by 2050

00:04:06.730 --> 00:04:09.880
and what they're gonna do in 2020 to 2030,

00:04:09.880 --> 00:04:12.680
to be down paying on that goal.

00:04:12.680 --> 00:04:14.170
If we can get the...

00:04:14.170 --> 00:04:15.420
If I say, the vast majority

00:04:15.420 --> 00:04:17.183
of nations taking that seriously,

00:04:18.070 --> 00:04:19.253
that is success.

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:22.440
Many scientists have said,

00:04:22.440 --> 00:04:25.730
the IPCC which is the UN scientific arm,

00:04:25.730 --> 00:04:27.210
that does the analysis,

00:04:27.210 --> 00:04:29.900
has said to us two years ago,

00:04:29.900 --> 00:04:33.410
we have about 12 years in front
of us within which to make

00:04:33.410 --> 00:04:37.020
the critical decisions necessary
to reduce the worst damage

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:38.430
from the climate crisis.

00:04:38.430 --> 00:04:41.060
So that's it, we've used
up two of those years,

00:04:41.060 --> 00:04:42.530
not enough happened.

00:04:42.530 --> 00:04:44.730
We now have about 10 years or so

00:04:44.730 --> 00:04:46.893
within which to get the job done.

